part records
  tally 1
  note "The record files of tmp/cases/A/records/ are not imported. Tally 1.0.1 reads records as rows of a movement input (L §5.18) brought by the importer (OPERATIONS §2.2), which names no dialect for a file with header lines above its column line, a day.month.year or day/month/year date, a decimal comma or a semicolon separator, and no way to read a fund register at all: a record is `movement CUR` (L §2.3), and a holding's units have no currency (observation O:A-1, O:A-2)."
  note "So this part holds only the joint-account rows the questions read by name (A-05, A-08, A-11), each in its own version with no covers, known on its booking day, its text citing its file and line; and the closing positions of 2025 as stated anchors (L §5.18). No version covers a place, so every aggregate of the records (A-09's balances and card average, A-10's) is guarded by covered() and is a hole."

index jrow: open
  note "rows of the joint account's statements (Bank Wrzos, LN27 … 0412)"

index jkind = [card_pay, card_refund, payback, standing, invest_move, own_move, tax_pay, other_in, other_out]
  note "the kinds A-HR1 v2 tells apart: card payments, card refunds, friends paying back shared bills, standing orders and instalments, the rule's own transfers, other own transfers, tax payments, anything else"

input jbank[r in jrow]: movement DUK (kind key jkind) question "What does this row of the joint account's statement say?"

